  bootwright / media list
      List the images this host stores with their sizes, recorded digests and the contexts that
      reserve them. The default reads records and file metadata only; --checksums reads every
      image in full and reports each computed digest and whether the image still matches its
      record.

  Usage
    bootwright media list [flags]

  Command flags
      --checksums  Compute image checksums

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  Examples
    bootwright media list --checksums
